  "question": {
    "text": "Taking Rydberg's constant $\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{H}}=1.097 \\times 10^{7} \\mathrm{~m}$, first and second wavelength of Balmer series in hydrogen spectrum is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "T38es",
      "text": "$2000 \\mathrm{~A}, 3000 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jG9y6",
      "text": "$1575 \\mathrm{~A}, 2960 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tVx4t",
      "text": "$6529 \\mathrm{~A}, 4280 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "g22Z4",
      "text": "$6552 \\mathrm{~A}, 4863 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\lambda}=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{1}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{2}^{2}}\\right]$. For first wavelength, $\\mathrm{n}_{1}$\n$$\n=2, \\mathrm{n}_{2}=3\n$$\n$\\Rightarrow \\lambda_{1}=6563 \\AA$. For second wavelength, $\\mathrm{n}_{1}$\n$=2, \\mathrm{n}_{2}=4 \\Rightarrow \\lambda_{2}=4861 \\AA$",
    "image": null
  },
